<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2TI" style="id">2 TIMOTHY</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2TI 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 1:1"/>
    Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by God’s sovereign choice and appointment, commissioned in accordance with the promise of eternal life that is available in Christ Jesus,
    <verse eid="2TI 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 1:2"/>
    To Timothy, my beloved spiritual son:
    <verse eid="2TI 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">May you experience grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and from Christ Jesus our Lord.</para>
  <para style="s1">Stir into Flame the Gift of God in You</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 1:3"/>
    I express gratitude to God, whom I worship with a conscience free from guilt just as my forefathers did, as I make mention of you constantly in my prayers both during the night hours and throughout the day.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 1:4"/>
    I am filled with longing to see you again, remembering the tears you shed at our parting, so that I might be filled with complete joy.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 1:5"/>
    I hold in my memory the sincere and authentic faith that resides in you, the same faith that first made its home in your grandmother Lois and in your mother Eunice, and I remain fully convinced that this faith now lives powerfully in you as well.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 1:6"/>
    It is for this very reason that I remind you to fan into flame and keep ablaze the spiritual gift that God placed within you when I laid my hands upon you in commissioning.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 1:7"/>
    For the Spirit that God has imparted to us does not produce cowardice or timidity, but rather produces power, love, and disciplined thinking.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Instructions for Timothy</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 1:8"/>
    So do not be embarrassed about bearing witness to our Lord, nor be ashamed of me who am imprisoned because of Him, but join with me in accepting hardship for the sake of the gospel, drawing strength from the power that God supplies,
    <verse eid="2TI 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 1:9"/>
    who has rescued us from condemnation and summoned us with a calling that is holy and set apart, not because of anything we have accomplished, but in accordance with His own predetermined plan and the grace He freely gave us in Christ Jesus from before the ages of time began,
    <verse eid="2TI 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 1:10"/>
    and this grace has now been openly revealed through the arrival of our Saviour Christ Jesus, who has abolished the power and authority of death and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 1:11"/>
    It is for the sake of this gospel that I was designated as a public proclaimer, as an apostle with authority, and as an instructor of truth.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 1:12"/>
    It is because of my commitment to this gospel that I am experiencing these present hardships, yet I feel no shame, for I have intimate knowledge of the One in whom I have invested my confidence, and I stand fully persuaded that He possesses the ability to safeguard what I have placed in His care until the day of His return.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 1:13"/>
    Maintain as your standard the collection of healthy teachings that you received from me, holding them in the context of the faith and love that are experienced in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 1:14"/>
    Protect the precious deposit of truth that has been entrusted to your care, doing so by the power of the Holy Spirit who makes His dwelling within us.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Household of Onesiphorus and Paul</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 1:15"/>
    You are aware of this reality, that all the believers in the province of Asia have abandoned me, and among these are Phygelus and Hermogenes.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 1:16"/>
    May the Lord extend compassion to the family of Onesiphorus, for he repeatedly brought refreshment to my spirit and felt no embarrassment about the chains I wear as a prisoner.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 1:17"/>
    On the contrary, when he came to the city of Rome, he pursued me with great determination until he located me.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 1:18"/>
    May the Lord allow him to experience divine mercy from the Lord on the day of final judgment. And you are thoroughly aware of the many ways he ministered to me during my time in Ephesus.
    <verse eid="2TI 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2TI 2"/>
  <para style="s1">Be Strong in God’s Grace</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 2:1"/>
    As for you, my spiritual son, you must continually draw your inner strength from the grace that flows from union with Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 2:2"/>
    The truths that you received from me in the hearing of numerous witnesses, these you must pass on and entrust to reliable individuals who will possess the capacity to teach still others.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 2:3"/>
    Accept your portion of suffering alongside me, conducting yourself as a well-trained soldier who belongs to Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 2:4"/>
    No soldier engaged in military service entangles himself in the everyday affairs and business pursuits of civilian life, for his objective is to satisfy and please the commanding officer who recruited him.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 2:5"/>
    In the same way, a competitor in athletic contests does not receive the winner’s crown unless he adheres strictly to the regulations governing the competition.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 2:6"/>
    The farmer who labours with dedication deserves to be the first to partake of the crops he has cultivated.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 2:7"/>
    Consider thoughtfully what I am communicating to you, for the Lord will provide you with insight and comprehension in all these things.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 2:8"/>
    Keep your mind continually focused on Jesus Christ, who was raised from death to life, who came from the lineage of David, exactly as my gospel message declares.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 2:9"/>
    It is on account of this gospel that I am experiencing affliction, to the extent of being confined with chains as though I were a dangerous criminal; yet the message of God is not subject to imprisonment or restraint.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 2:10"/>
    Therefore I willingly bear all things for the benefit of those whom God has chosen, so that they as well might attain the deliverance that comes through Christ Jesus, accompanied by glory that lasts forever.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 2:11"/>
    This statement deserves complete trust and confidence:
    <verse eid="2TI 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">For if we have experienced death in union with Him,</para>
  <para style="p">we shall also experience life in union with Him;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 2:12"/>
    if we persevere through trials with endurance,
    <verse eid="2TI 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">we shall also exercise royal authority alongside Him;</para>
  <para style="p">if we repudiate Him,</para>
  <para style="p">He likewise will repudiate us;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 2:13"/>
    if we demonstrate unfaithfulness,
    <verse eid="2TI 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">He continues to demonstrate faithfulness,</para>
  <para style="p">for it is impossible for Him to act contrary to His own character.</para>
  <para style="s1">Present Yourself Approved to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 2:14"/>
    Continue to bring these truths to the remembrance of the brothers and sisters, giving them solemn warning in God’s presence not to quarrel about words, a practice that accomplishes no beneficial purpose and leads to the spiritual destruction of those who hear such arguments.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 2:15"/>
    Give diligent effort to offer yourself to God as one who has passed the test and received approval, as a labourer who has no cause for shame, who correctly interprets and accurately communicates the message of truth.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 2:16"/>
    But keep yourself distant from godless and meaningless chatter, for those who engage in it will advance further and further into ungodly living,
    <verse eid="2TI 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 2:17"/>
    and their false teaching will consume and spread like a gangrenous infection. Among these false teachers are Hymenaeus and Philetus.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 2:18"/>
    These men have deviated from the truth by asserting that the resurrection of believers has already taken place in the past, and by this claim they are undermining and destroying the faith of certain individuals.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2TI 2:19"/>
    Yet despite this, the solid foundation that God has laid remains unshaken and stable, marked with this inscription: “The Lord recognises and knows intimately those who truly belong to Him,” and, “Let everyone who calls upon the Lord’s name separate himself from wickedness and injustice.”
    <verse eid="2TI 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2TI 2:20"/>
    Now in a large and wealthy house there exist not only containers fashioned from gold and silver, but also containers made from wood and earthenware, and some are designated for noble purposes while others serve common or degrading functions.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2TI 2:21"/>
    So if anyone purifies himself by removing himself from what is ignoble and dishonourable, he will become a vessel designated for honourable use, consecrated and set apart, valuable and useful to the Master of the house, and fully prepared and equipped for every kind of good work.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2TI 2:22"/>
    Run away from the desires and impulses characteristic of youth, and instead pursue after righteousness, faithful trust, self-giving love, and harmony with others, doing so in company with those who invoke the Lord’s name from hearts that are pure and sincere.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="2TI 2:23"/>
    Turn away from and refuse to engage in foolish speculations and ignorant debates, because you understand that these generate conflicts and quarrels.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:23"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="2TI 2:24"/>
    And a servant who belongs to the Lord must not be characterised by a contentious spirit, but instead must demonstrate kindness towards all people, must possess the ability to communicate truth effectively, must show patience when he is mistreated or insulted,
    <verse eid="2TI 2:24"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="2TI 2:25"/>
    instructing those who stand in opposition with a spirit of gentleness and humility, hoping that perhaps God will grant them a change of mind that leads to full recognition of the truth,
    <verse eid="2TI 2:25"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="2TI 2:26"/>
    and that they will return to their right senses and break free from the trap the devil has set, having been held captive by him to carry out his purposes.
    <verse eid="2TI 2:26"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2TI 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Difficult Times in the Last Days</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 3:1"/>
    You must grasp this truth clearly: During the concluding era of human history there will be periods characterised by extreme difficulty and dangerous conditions.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 3:2"/>
    For people will be entirely absorbed in love for themselves and obsessed with accumulating wealth, they will be characterised by arrogant boasting and haughty pride, they will engage in blasphemous speech and slander, they will show rebellious disobedience toward their parents, they will lack gratitude, and they will have no regard for what is holy.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 3:3"/>
    They will be devoid of natural family affection, they will refuse to make peace or reach agreements, they will spread false and slanderous accusations, they will have no ability to exercise self-control, they will be savage and cruel in disposition, and they will hate what is morally good.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 3:4"/>
    They will betray confidences and commitments, they will act rashly without thinking, they will be puffed up with conceit and self-importance, they will be devoted to pursuing pleasurable experiences rather than being devoted to God,
    <verse eid="2TI 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 3:5"/>
    they will maintain an external form or appearance of godly religion while having rejected and denied the power that could genuinely transform them. You must avoid such people and keep yourself separate from them.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 3:6"/>
    For within this category are those who use cunning methods to enter into households and manipulate weak-willed women who are weighed down by accumulated sins and controlled by all kinds of passions and cravings,
    <verse eid="2TI 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 3:7"/>
    women who are perpetually learning new teachings yet never capable of coming to full and accurate knowledge of the truth.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 3:8"/>
    In the same manner that Jannes and Jambres stood in opposition to Moses, these individuals also stand against the truth. They are people whose minds have become morally corrupted and perverted, and regarding genuine faith they have failed the test and been rejected as counterfeit.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 3:9"/>
    However, they will not continue to make headway in their deception, for their senseless foolishness will become completely obvious and apparent to everyone, just as happened with those two magicians who opposed Moses.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">The Man of God and the Scripture</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 3:10"/>
    But you have followed closely and traced carefully my teaching, my manner of life, my resolute purpose, my faith and trust, my patience under trial, my love, my steadfast endurance,
    <verse eid="2TI 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 3:11"/>
    along with the persecutions and the sufferings that I experienced in Antioch, in Iconium, and in Lystra. You witnessed firsthand what severe persecutions I endured, yet from every one of them the Lord brought me safely through to deliverance.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 3:12"/>
    In fact, all those who are determined to live lives characterised by godliness in union with Christ Jesus will experience persecution and opposition.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 3:13"/>
    But evil individuals and fraudulent imposters will proceed from bad conditions to worse, leading others into error while they themselves are being led astray.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 3:14"/>
    As for you, however, you must continue to stand firm in the truths you have learned and have become fully convinced of, keeping in mind the trustworthy character of the people from whom you learned these things,
    <verse eid="2TI 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 3:15"/>
    and bearing in mind that from your earliest childhood you have had knowledge of the sacred writings, which possess the power to make you wise and lead you to salvation through the faith that is placed in Christ Jesus.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 3:16"/>
    All Scripture originates from God’s own breath, and it serves a beneficial purpose for teaching, for exposing and refuting error, for correcting what is wrong, and for providing training and discipline in living a righteous life,
    <verse eid="2TI 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 3:17"/>
    so that the man of God may be brought to perfection or complete maturity, fully equipped for the accomplishment of every kind of good work.
    <verse eid="2TI 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="2TI 4"/>
  <para style="s1">Preach the Word</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TI 4:1"/>
    I charge you in the sight of God and of Christ Jesus, who will one day serve as judge over those who are living and those who have died, and I charge you in view of His future appearance and His coming kingdom:
    <verse eid="2TI 4:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TI 4:2"/>
    Proclaim the message of God’s word with urgency and persistence. Maintain readiness to minister whether the circumstances appear opportune or inopportune. Use the Scriptures to expose and refute error, to issue strong warnings against sin, and to appeal for obedience, always exercising great patience and providing thorough instruction.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TI 4:3"/>
    For the time is approaching when people will refuse to put up with or tolerate wholesome teaching that promotes spiritual health. Rather, motivated by their own selfish desires and cravings, they will accumulate for themselves a multitude of teachers who will say precisely what their itching ears want to hear,
    <verse eid="2TI 4:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TI 4:4"/>
    and they will deliberately turn their attention away from the truth and will allow themselves to be led off course towards myths and fabricated tales.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TI 4:5"/>
    But as for you, maintain sober judgment and self-control under all circumstances. Be willing to accept and endure hardship. Perform the work that an evangelist does in proclaiming the gospel. Carry through to completion all the responsibilities of your ministry.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul Finishes the Race</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TI 4:6"/>
    For my own life is already in the process of being poured out like a drink offering on an altar, and the time of my departure from this life has arrived and stands near.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TI 4:7"/>
    I have fought the good fight with courage and determination, I have run the entire race that was set before me and reached the finish line, and I have kept and maintained the faith that was entrusted to me.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TI 4:8"/>
    From this time forward there is reserved and waiting for me the victor’s crown that is awarded on the basis of righteousness, which the Lord, who judges with perfect justice, will present to me on that final day, and He will give it not only to me but to all those who have loved and eagerly anticipated His appearing.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul Abandoned</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TI 4:9"/>
    Do everything within your power to come to me quickly and without delay.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TI 4:10"/>
    For Demas has abandoned me because he fell in love with this present world system and its attractions, and he has travelled to Thessalonica. Crescens has departed for Galatia, and Titus has gone to Dalmatia.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TI 4:11"/>
    Luke is the only one who remains here with me at present. Take Mark and bring him along with you when you come, for he proves himself useful and helpful to me in carrying out the work of ministry.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TI 4:12"/>
    I have sent Tychicus to the city of Ephesus on a mission.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TI 4:13"/>
    When you make your journey here, bring with you the heavy cloak that I left behind in Troas with Carpus, and also bring the scrolls containing Scripture, but especially bring the parchment documents.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TI 4:14"/>
    Alexander, the worker in metal, inflicted much harm and injury upon me. The Lord will render to him the recompense his actions deserve.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TI 4:15"/>
    You also should be on your guard concerning him, for he vigorously resisted our teaching.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TI 4:16"/>
    When I made my first defence before the Roman authorities, not a single person came to stand beside me in support, but instead everyone abandoned me. May this failure not be charged against them.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Paul’s Confidence in the Lord</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TI 4:17"/>
    But the Lord took His position at my side and infused me with strength, so that through my testimony the proclamation of the gospel might be brought to full completion and all the Gentile nations might have the opportunity to hear it. And in this manner I was rescued out of the lion’s mouth and from mortal danger.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TI 4:18"/>
    The Lord will continue to rescue me from every scheme of evil, and He will preserve me safely for entrance into His heavenly kingdom. To Him belongs the glory throughout all the ages to come. Amen.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Final Greetings</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2TI 4:19"/>
    Extend my greetings to Prisca and Aquila, and to all those who belong to the household of Onesiphorus.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2TI 4:20"/>
    Erastus has remained in the city of Corinth, but I was compelled to leave Trophimus behind in Miletus because he had fallen sick with illness.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2TI 4:21"/>
    Make every effort to arrive here before the winter season sets in. Eubulus sends his greetings to you, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers and sisters here.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2TI 4:22"/>
    May the Lord be present with your spirit. May grace be with all of you.
    <verse eid="2TI 4:22"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TI 4"/>
</usx>
